      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is twice that limit, and it raises the risk of serious lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nI suspect a transcription error. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at some frequency, if that's what you meant.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and add a note with the clinical rationale. I would still want you to confirm it before I enter it."
      }
     ],
